meta {
  name: Create Order - Order Discount On Non-Discountable Test (201)
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "ORDER",
    "orderDate": "2026-10-14",
    "orderType": "WALK_IN",
    "billingType": "CASH_CLIENT",
    "patientId": "{{patientId}}",
    "items": [
      {
        "branchLabTestId": "{{branchLabTestId}}"
      }
    ],
    "payments": [
      {
        "totalAmount": 1000,
        "orderDiscount": 150,
        "orderDiscountMode": "AMOUNT",
        "orderDiscountValue": 150,
        "netAmount": 850,
        "payableAmount": 850,
        "paidAmount": 850,
        "paymentMode": "CASH"
      }
    ]
  }
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });
  test("order-level discount is applied even on a non-discountable test", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d.discountAmount).to.equal(150);
    expect(d.netAmount).to.equal(850);
  });
}

docs {
  Regression for the per-test "Allow Discounts" rule: an **order-level** discount
  (`payments[].orderDiscount`) is accepted **regardless** of a test's catalogue
  `isAllowDiscounts` flag — the per-test rule restricts only **per-line** item
  discounts (`items[].discount`), never the order-level discount.

  Point `{{branchLabTestId}}` at a branch lab test whose source Master Data test
  has `Allow Discounts = No`. The order succeeds (201); the order's net reflects
  the ₹150 order discount, and that discount is allocated proportionally across
  the order's lines (including the non-discountable test) in the billing/report
  breakdown. Contrast with `Create Order - Test Discount Not Allowed (422)`, where
  a **per-line** discount on the same test is rejected.

  Behaviour matrix (verified):
  - Allow Discounts = No  + order-level discount → **201** (this request)
  - Allow Discounts = No  + per-line item discount → **422 TEST_DISCOUNT_NOT_ALLOWED**
  - Allow Discounts = Yes + per-line item discount → **201** (within branch min/max %)
}
